  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1241 PM MDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nThe dry and warming pattern will persist through tomorrow as high \npressure remains in control over the region. Expect daytime \ntemperatures to warm into the upper 70s to low 80s across low \nelevations today and tomorrow.\n\nAn upper-level trough will work eastward with the accompanying cold \nfront bringing breezy to windy conditions tomorrow. The strongest \nwinds will be across the central mountains and eastern Magic Valley, \nwhere gusts will largely range 30 to 40 mph, while gusts will \ngenerally range 20 to 30 mph further east. Precipitation will remain \nfurther north outside of our CWA. Temperatures will run much cooler \nbehind the front, with highs returning to the 60s and low 70s during \nthe weekend.\n\nThe next Pacific trough will move onshore Sunday, bringing\nisolated showers and thunderstorms to eastern Idaho late Sunday\nthrough Monday evening. Expect a 5 to 10 degree cooldown for \nmost locations between Sunday and Monday, sending daytime highs \ndown into the 50s and 60s. Ensembles suggest weak high pressure \nbuilding in from the west beginning Tuesday, keeping conditions \ndry and allowing temperatures to very gradually warm through \nlater week. That said, daytime temperatures will still run below\naverage during this timeframe.",
